1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Iry-Hor or Ro (as read by Petrie) was a Predynastic pharaoh of ancient Egypt, although some archaeologists are doubtful of his existence. He was most likely Ka's immediate predecessor. He ruled over Abydos and was 
2 CONC buried in its local cemetery at Umm el-Qa'ab near Ka, Narmer and the First Dynasty kings.
2 CONT
2 CONT The argument against his existence rests on the lack of a serekh in front of his name and the poor attestation. The only other inscription of Iry-Hor outside of Abydos is located in Lower Egypt, while Ka and Narmer have many inscr
2 CONC iptions located as far as Israel. Toby Wilkinson dismisses the tomb as a storage pit and the name as a treasury mark.
2 CONT
2 CONT Supporters point to the size and location of the tomb. It is a double tomb as big as Ka's and Narmer's, located within a sequential order linking the older "U" cemetery with the First Dynasty tombs. The name is inscribed on a larg
2 CONC e jar, like that of other pharaohs, and contains the royal Horus falcon. The serekh could have been a tradition that started with Ka.
