1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ka, also Sekhem Ka, was a predynastic pharaoh of Upper Egypt. Ka means "soul". This is a name for a part of a soul in Egyptian religion. Ka ruled over Abydos in the late 32nd or early 31st century BC and was buried
2 CONC  at Umm el-Qa'ab. He most likely was the immediate successor to Iry-Hor and was succeeded by Narmer. He is the earliest known Egyptian king with a serekh, inscribed on a number of artifacts.
