1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semiramis
2 CONT The Two Babylons records Semiramis as being BOTH the mother AND husband of Nimrod/Ninus.
2 CONT She was pregnant at the time King Nimrod was executed for blasphemy by Noah''s son Shem, and when she gave birth to a son, whom she named Tammuz, she claimed that it was a virgin birth, and that Tammuz was the rebirth of Nimrod wh
2 CONC om she claimed had become the sun god and she the moon goddess. Her image of her religion (a woman holding a baby boy, the crescent moon over her head or under her feet, and the sun or "halo" over the head of the child) spread thr
2 CONC oughout the world, with Nimrod/Tammuz/Semiramis becoming Isis & Horus & Set in Egypt, Ba'al & Dagon & Atargatis in Canaan, Odin & Thor & Jord in Scandinavia, Hu (Maki) & Pan & Britannia in Britain, Vishnu & Shiva & Devi in Hinduis
2 CONC m, Zeus & Hera & Apollo, Jupiter & Juno & Vulcan in Rome, etc. Constantine the Great combined all of these deities, and with his creation of Roman Catholicism in the 4th century applied the Hebrew Christian names of Mary and Jesus
2 CONC  to the idol of the mother & child image of Semiramis and Tammuz.
2 CONT
2 CONT Event(s)
2 CONT Birth: BC, EREC, NINIVEH, CALDEA-ASIRIA, MESOPOTAMIA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: BC, UR, BABeLONIA, CALDEA-ASIRIA, MESOPOTAMIA
