2 CONC lermo is damaged at that place and only short note of his coming to the rule and first year of rule are readable. Possibly he held his predecessor Semerkhet as usurper because he ordered to destroy his names while the name of his 
2 CONC own father, Anedjib, left untouched (J. von Beckerath). N. Grimal s point of view Qa a was father of Semerkhet. Tomb of Qa a is located at Abydos (tomb Q) and had been greatly extended. Mortuary complex at Saqqara is the first in 
2 CONC Egyptian history which includes mortuary temple, which became the indispensable part of sacral complex of each ruler ever since.
