1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Meret-Isesi (also Mereret-Isesi; "Beloved by Isesi") was a Princess of Egypt, and she lived during 5th dynasty. Her father was Pharaoh Djedkare. Meret-Isesi appears as a King's daughter of his body in a relief whic
2 CONC h likely comes from Abusir. The relief can be found on the Brooklyn Museum page for Mereret-Isesi. The caption identifies this princess as Kekheretnebti (she was a sister of Mereret-Isesi), but the text clearly identifies her as M
2 CONC ereret-Isesi.
