2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Pharaoh of Egypt 
2 CONT
2 CONT Reign 1550–1525 BC (disputed)
2 CONT
2 CONT 25 years in Manetho,  18th Dynasty 
2 CONT
2 CONT Predecessor Kamose (Upper Egypt), Khamudi (Lower Egypt) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Successor Amenhotep I 
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal titulary[show]Prenomen: Nebpehtire[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lord of Strength is Re  
2 CONT
2 CONT Nomen: Ahmose[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Born of the moon or Born of Yah 
2 CONT
2 CONT Horus name: Aakheperu[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Great of Developments[5] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nebty name: Tutmesut[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Perfect of Birth[5] 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Golden Horus: Tjestawy[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT He who Knots Together the Two Lands[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Consort(s) Ahmose-Nefertari, God's Wife of Amun, Ahmose-Sitkamose 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Meritamen, Sitamun, Siamun, Ahmose-ankh, Amenhotep I, Ramose, possibly Mutnofret 
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Tao II Seqenenre 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother Ahhotep I 
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1525 BC 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Mummy found in Deir el-Bahri cache, but was likely originally buried in Abydos 
2 CONT
2 CONT Monuments Palace at Avaris, Temple of Amun at Karnak, Temple of Montu at Armant 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ahmose I (sometimes written Amosis I and "Amenes" and meaning Born of the Moon or Born of Yah) was a pharaoh of ancient Egypt and the founder of the Eighteenth dynasty. He was a member of the Theban royal house, the son of pharaoh
2 CONC  Tao II Seqenenre and brother of the last pharaoh of the Seventeenth dynasty, King Kamose. Sometime during the reign of his father or grandfather, Thebes rebelled against the Hyksos, the rulers of Lower Egypt. When he was seven hi
2 CONC s father was killed,[6] and he was about ten when his brother died of unknown causes, after reigning only three years. Ahmose I assumed the throne after the death of his brother,[7] and upon coronation became known as Neb-Pehty-Re
2 CONC  (The Lord of Strength is Re).
2 CONT
2 CONT During his reign, he completed the conquest and expulsion of the Hyksos from the delta region, restored Theban rule over the whole of Egypt and successfully reasserted Egyptian power in its formerly subject territories of Nubia an
2 CONC d Canaan.[7] He then reorganized the administration of the country, reopened quarries, mines and trade routes and began massive construction projects of a type that had not been undertaken since the time of the Middle Kingdom. Thi
2 CONC s building program culminated in the construction of the last pyramid built by native Egyptian rulers. Ahmose's reign laid the foundations for the New Kingdom, under which Egyptian power reached its peak. His reign is usually date
2 CONC d to about 1550–1525 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents [hide]
2 CONT
