1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Hui (priestess)
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Hui was an ancient Egyptian priestess during the 18th dynasty. She was the mother of Merytre-Hatshepsut, the Great Royal Wife of Pharaoh Thutmose III.[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Hui played an important role in the cults of Amun, Ra and Atum. One of her statues was found, it names her as the mother of the Great Royal Wife. This proves that Merytre was not the daughter of Queen Hatshepsut, as she was though
2 CONC t to be. (Thutmose's other Great Royal Wife, Satiah, is known to be the daughter of a royal nurse named Ipu.) The statue, which is now in the British Museum, also depicts the children of Thutmose and Merytre, except for Amenhotep 
2 CONC II. Princess Nebetiunet is sitting on her grandmother's lap, Prince Menkheperre and princesses Meritamen, the other Meritamen and Iset can be seen on the side of the statue. Iset was probably the youngest, as her figure is much sm
2 CONC aller than that of the others.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hui_(priestess)
