1 NOTE known reign 3 yr 10 mo 26 days
2 CONT the first part of his reign he was under the control of he older half
2 CONT sister Hatshepsut and upon her death in about 1494 he ordered all of
2 CONT her monuments altered as if she had never existed. He went on a series of military conquests that took Egypt to the largest territory ever to that point.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thuthmose III has a fixed reignal date, the start can be either 1490 or 1504 BC from a series of Lunar obsservations.  This is discussed at length by Lee W Casperson in JNES (Journal Near East Studies) p 139 -150 (following R A Pa
2 CONC rker's 1957 article) NES 16(1957)p39/43 and CAH. Casperson concludes as do I that 1504 is correct. But there is an even stronger argument in that by including the known Rising of Sirus dates from 1539 BC (CAH corrected from 1543 o
2 CONC riginal calculation) in 9th year 9th day third dseason of Amenhotep I and known reignal years months and days (DB Redford JNES 25(1966) p53 (but his dates are in error keyed to 1290 date of Ramses II, and totaly witout Siarus or l
2 CONC unar observations = add 14 years) the 1490 becomes impossible.  Thus we know the day and month of accession, and this gives us the year, 19 May 1504 BC.  Thuthmose III died day 30 of month VII thus we have another check fixed date
2 CONC .
2 CONT Fixed date Ramses II of 1304 from Lunar new moon festival in 52 Ramese II
2 CONT see Ramses II for details, also CAH (Cambridge Ancient History)
2 CONT
2 CONT There was a Lunar Eclipse recorded in 14 Takelot which was 24 Feb 822 BC.
2 CONT This fixes the reign to 836 start date. JNES Vol 24 p 61 (1967)
