1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://miriamhakedosha.blogspot.com/2012/05/judith-jewish-queen-empress-of-ethiopia.html
2 CONT
2 CONT This research has been done by DNA research
2 CONT
2 CONT High-Queen Asenath the Beautiful (Isnetnofret/ Istnofret/ Anath /Osnat/ Bat Sokhota) of Rhoda and Princess of Judah (b. 465) (H2 mt-dna) [Sister of Princess Tamar Tia of Tahpahnes (Tephi) (H1 mt-dna)] married Nilius (Nimlot/ Niall
2 CONC / Nel/ Nili Mu) Milesian Prince of Thebes son of Osorkon II (Osorkor/ Sokar/ Socho)
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT I am a fifth generation Australian of Anglo Jewish ancestry who belongs to the R1b M222+ subclade of A260 y-dna and to I1a1 mt-dna clade. My father belongs to J1b1a1 mt-dna and my mother's father belongs to R1b SYR2627 y-dna. I ha
2 CONC ve a Bachelor of Arts (majoring in History and minoring in English Literature, Ancient History and Music) from the University of Western Australia, a Graduate Diploma of Education (History, English and Religion) from the Australia
2 CONC n Catholic University and a Master of Arts (in Theological Studies) from the University of Notre Dame.
2 CONT
2 CONT This blog is to share some of my insights drawn from over 30 or so years of research. Three major influences in the area of history on me have been the writings of Immanuel Velikovsky, Cecil Roth and Arthur Zuckerman. In my younge
2 CONC r year, I was also inspired in the area of genealogy and heraldry by Leslie Gilbert Pine and Sir Iain Moncreiffe and did a course in Genealogy and Heraldry with Dr Douglas Sutherland-Bruce at UWA. 
