2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Amenhotep II
2 CONT
2 CONT Amenophis II
2 CONT
2 CONT Pharaoh of Egypt
2 CONT
2 CONT Reign	1427–1401 BC or 1427–1397 BC,  18th Dynasty
2 CONT
2 CONT Predecessor	Thutmose III
2 CONT
2 CONT Successor	Thutmose IV
2 CONT
2 CONT Royal titulary[show]
2 CONT
2 CONT Consort(s)	Tiaa
2 CONT
2 CONT Children	Thutmose IV, Amenhotep, Webensenu, Amenemopet, Nedjem, Khaemwaset?, Aaheperkare? Aakheperure? Iaret, Ahmose (?)
2 CONT
2 CONT Father	Thutmose III
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother	Merytre-Hatshepsut
2 CONT
2 CONT Died	1401 or 1397 BC
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial	KV35
2 CONT
2 CONT Amenhotep II (sometimes read as Amenophis II and meaning Amun is Satisfied) was the seventh Pharaoh of the 18th dynasty of Egypt. Amenhotep inherited a vast kingdom from his father Thutmose III, and held it by means of a few milit
2 CONC ary campaigns in Syria; however, he fought much less than his father, and his reign saw the effective cessation of hostilities between Egypt and Mitanni, the major kingdoms vying for power in Syria. His reign is usually dated from
2 CONC  1427 to 1400 BC.
2 CONT
