1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Tiaa
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT For other meanings, see Tiaa (disambiguation).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Tiaa or Tia'a was an Ancient Egyptian queen during the eighteenth dynasty of Egypt. She was the wife of Pharaoh Amenhotep II and the mother of Thutmose IV[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT She is never called king's daughter, and thus her parentage is unknown. It has been speculated that she was Amenhotep's sister or half sister, but it is not certain.[2] During the reign of her husband the women of the royal family
2 CONC  were much less represented than earlier during the 18h dynasty; this was probably because the pharaoh did not want any of them usurp power as Hatshepsut had only a few decades earlier.[3]. Tiaa is the only known wife of Amenhotep
2 CONC , and her name is known to us only because she was the mother of the next pharaoh, Thutmose IV. She received the title of Great Royal Wife during her son's reign; in her husband's lifetime it was borne only by Amenhotep's mother M
2 CONC erytre-Hatshepsut[3].
2 CONT
2 CONT Tiaa is not depicted on any monuments built by her husband, only on those which were completed by her son. During the reign of Thutmose IV she rose to more prominence; along with the title of Great Royal Wife she also received the
2 CONC  titles King's Mother and God's Wife. On many statues she and Thutmose's first chief wife Nefertari accompany the pharaoh[4]. Several depictions of Merytre-Hatshepsut were altered to show Tiaa.[5]. One of Thutmose's daughter, Tiaa
2 CONC  is likely to have been named after her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tiaa was buried in the tomb KV32 in the Valley of the Kings, where fragments of her funerary equipment were found. Floodwater washed some of these into KV47, the adjacent 19th dynasty tomb of Pharaoh Siptah, causing Egyptologists 
2 CONC to believe they belong to a like-named mother of Siptah[1][6], however, since then Siptah's mother has been identified as a Syrian concubine named Sutailja.
2 CONT
2 CONT Forrás / Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiaa
2 CONT
2 CONT Lásd még / See other website
2 CONT
