1 NOTE He reigned 1386-1349 BC, of the 18th Dynasty, builder of extensive 
2 CONT architectural works, including portions of the temple of Luxor and the 
2 CONT so-called Colossi of Memnon. His reign was one of peace and prosperity, 
2 CONT when Egyptian power was at its height. Amenhotep's diplomatic 
2 CONT correspondence is preserved in the Amarna Letters, a collection of some 
2 CONT 400 clay tablets found in Tell el-Amarna in 1887. Ikhnaton, Egypt's great 
2 CONT religious reformer, was his son.
