1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =From [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osorkon_IV Wikipedia]=
2 CONT Osorkon IV was a ruler of Lower Egypt who, while not always listed as a member of the Twenty-second dynasty of Egypt, he is attested as the ruler of Tanis, and thereby one of Shoshenq V's successors. Therefore he is sometimes list
2 CONC ed as part of the dynasty, whether for convenience or in fact.
2 CONT
2 CONT His parentage is uncertain: he could be a son of Shoshenq V. His mother, named on an electrum headpiece in the Louvre, is Tadibast III.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Reign==
2 CONT Kenneth Kitchen gives Osorkon IV's reign dates as 732/30 – 716 BC.
2 CONT
2 CONT Osorkon's reign was never recognised at Memphis where documents were dated to the reign of 24th Saite dynasty king Bakenranef. During his time, Egypt was ruled concurrently by four dynasties – the 22nd, 23rd, 24th and the 25th. Sh
2 CONC ortly after Osorkon had ascended the throne, Upper Egypt was conquered by the Kushite king, Piankhi, and Osorkon IV ended ruling only the East Nile Delta region.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Relationship with Assyria==
2 CONT He is perhaps mentioned in the bible as the Pharaoh "So" to whom Hoshea, King of Israel appealed for help. However, So dispatched no aid or troops. The Israelite capital Samaria was captured by the Assyrian king Shalmaneser V in 7
2 CONC 22 BC and its inhabitants were imprisoned and taken to exile in Assyria and Media. To avoid military conflict with the Assyrians or even invasion, Osorkon sent presents, including several horses, to placate the new Assyrian king S
2 CONC argon II, who rose to power later in 722. Osorkon's tactic apparently worked, since Sargon accepted his gifts and did not take action against him.
2 CONT
2 CONT =From [http://ancient_egypt.enacademic.com/915/Osorkon_IV Academic Encyclopedias and Dictionaries]=
2 CONT  Throne name possibly Aakheperre setepenamun. He was probably the last ruler of Dynasty 22and ruled only in the areas of Tanisand Bubastis. He is named on the stelaof Piyeand attested in Assyrian sources in 716 BC. He may be the r
2 CONC uler who appears in the Bible as So, king of Egypt. He was followed by the Nubian rulers of Dynasty 25.
