1 NOTE Egyptian pharaoh of the 18th dynasty, the son-in-law of Ikhnaton, whom he 
2 CONT succeeded. He became pharoah at about the age of 9 and ruled until his 
2 CONT death at about the age of 18. Peace was brought to Egypt during his reign 
2 CONT as the worship of Amon, abandoned under Ikhnaton, was restored and Thebes, 
2 CONT the city sacred to Amon, was again made Egypt's capital. Although he was 
2 CONT not an important king, Tutankhamen is well known today because his tomb, 
2 CONT containing fabulous treasures, was found virtually intact by the British 
2 CONT archaeologists Howard Carter and Lord Carnarvon in 1922.
