1 NOTE DSI : Son of Nekau II and queen Khedebnetiretbinet. During short time of his reign he had lead expedition against Nubians as documented in stele inscriptions and by  Herodotus. Results of this expedition are not clear to us. It is
2 CONC  known that in one of the battles great number of Nubians was brought to death and 4200 of others were captured. It is not known whether the capital at Napata was conquered. Of Psametik period of rule survived numerous artifacts, 
2 CONC he was decorating buildings with tiny architectonic accents, lot of edifices he erected himself, lot of them just usurped.  He died in his way back from Phoenicia.
