2 CONT Pharaoh 589-570 BC
1 NOTE DSI : Son of Psametik II. Energetic and brave ruler.  He warred with Phoenites, captured Sydon and for 13 years laid siege to Thyr. He supported Jewish uprising against Babylon which ended up with a conflict with Nabuchodonozor. I
2 CONC n 586 BC Jerusalem had been captured by Babylonians. Under Apries the Jewish community on Elephantine arose. Due to revolt in his army in 569 BC he lost his function, captured by Amasis, next handed over to populace and strangled.
2 CONC  Another version tells that Aproes was brought to death in march 22, 569 BC during the battle of Amasis army with Nabuchodonozor, where he supported probably Babylonians. According to  Herodotus, Apries was buried by Amasis in the
2 CONC  temple-tombs at Sais.
1 NOTE OR "UAHIBRE""UAPHRIS""APRIES""HOPHRA"; PER-'O 589-570 BC; DEFEATED THE
2 CONT PHOENICIANS IN A GREAT SEA BATTLE; WENT TO THE RESCUE OF JERUSALEM ca. 588 BC
2 CONT (MENTIONED IN JERMEMIAH 44:30)
