0 @N6000000002187610059@ NOTE Antef VII
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Antef VII (or Nubkheperre Intef) was an Egyptian king of the Seventeenth dynasty of Egypt, and therefore ruled during the Second Intermediate Period, when Egypt was ruled by multiple kings.
1 CONT
1 CONT He ruled from Thebes, and was buried in a tomb in the necropolis of Dra' Abu el-Naga'. The grave was originally covered with a small pyramid (approximately 11 m at the base, rising to a height of approx. 13 m.) Auguste Mariette fo
1 CONC und two broken obelisks with complete Fivefold Titulary, which was then subsequently lost on transport to the Cairo Museum.
1 CONT [edit]
1 CONT
