0 @N6000000002187608829@ NOTE Ahmose I
1 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
1 CONT
1 CONT Aakheperu[2]
1 CONT Reign 1550 BC to 1525 BC (though disputed)
1 CONT 25 years in Manetho
1 CONT Consort(s) Ahmose-Nefertari
1 CONT God's Wife of Amun
1 CONT Issues Meretamun B, Sitamun A,
1 CONT Siamun A, Ahmose-anhk,
1 CONT Amenhotep I, Ramose A,
1 CONT possibly Mutneferet A
1 CONT Father Tao II Seqenenre
1 CONT Mother Ahhotep
1 CONT Died 1525 BC
1 CONT Burial Mummy found in Deir el-Bahri cache,
1 CONT but was likely originally buried in Abydos
1 CONT Major
1 CONT Monuments Palace at Avaris,
1 CONT Temple of Amun at Karnak,
1 CONT Temple of Monthu at Armant
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Ahmose I (also known as Amosis I) was a pharaoh of ancient Egypt and the founder of the Eighteenth dynasty. During his reign he conquered the Hyksos and restored Theban rule over all of Egypt, and was also successful in reassertin
1 CONC g Egyptian power in its formerly subject territories of Nubia and Canaan.[3] He then reorganized the administration of the country, reopened quarries, mines, and trade routes, and began massive construction projects like had not b
1 CONC een done since the Middle Kingdom. This laid the foundations for the New Kingdom, under which Egyptian power reached its peak. His reign is usually dated to about 1550-1525 BC.
1 CONT
1 CONT Ahmose was the son of king Tao II Seqenenre and brother of king Kamose, the last king of the Seventeenth dynasty. At the age of 10, Ahmose I (The Moon is Born) assumed the throne after the death of his brother, who died after reig
1 CONC ning only three years.[4] Upon assuming the crown, he became known as Neb-pehty-re (The Lord of Strength is Re).
1 CONT Contents
1 CONT [hide]
1 CONT
1 CONT     * 1 Family
1 CONT     * 2 Dates and length of reign
1 CONT     * 3 Campaigns
1 CONT     * 4 Art and monumental constructions
1 CONT           o 4.1 Pyramid
1 CONT     * 5 Mummy
